Gut reaction: honestly, most of these would wash over me. The graphic medical photos might make me wince for a second, but I've seen plenty of scary stuff on the telly and it doesn't change what I put in the basket. Calorie badges I'd probably notice, but I don't count calories, and Keith's reduced shelf is going to beat any label when I'm standing at the counter with forty quid's worth of bills in my head. The plain text ones are just more small print to me.

Right, allocating. Nothing's going to make me swap a Dairy Milk for a beetroot crisp on a whim, but if anything gets a look it's the calorie badge sitting next to the price, since that's the sort of thing that actually stands out when you're choosing. I'd give most of the points to F and E, a few to B, and almost nothing to the bare warnings or the plain shop shelf.

