Gut reaction: I'd barely look at any of these. The calorie badges are just numbers I'd have to do sums with, and I'm not counting anything when I'm hungry at nine at night. The gory photos would probably make me look away and then grab what I wanted anyway, and the black-and-white warnings read like something off a cigarette packet that I've stopped noticing. Honestly the only thing that would nudge me is the reduced shelf and whether the cheaper option is sitting right there.

Points: the calorie-badge ones get a bit more because at least they're information I could use if I was in the shop, but not much.

